{
  "program": "COUSR02C",
  "caseId": "case10",
  "description": "The fourth of UPDATE-USER-INFO's four independent change tests, at app/cbl/COUSR02C.cbl:231-234, and the folder's proof that COUSR02C performs NO validation of SEC-USR-TYPE.\n\nThe new type is 'X'. That matters: COCOM01Y declares only two condition names for a user type, CDEMO-USRTYP-ADMIN VALUE 'A' and CDEMO-USRTYP-USER VALUE 'U', and COUSR02C tests neither here. It compares USRTYPEI with SEC-USR-TYPE, and if they differ it moves the new byte in and sets USR-MODIFIED-YES - no membership test, no case folding, no rejection. Writing a VALID type would leave that unproven, because a translation that quietly validated the field would accept 'A' and still pass. With 'X' the assertion has teeth: the byte is persisted verbatim at offset 56 of the USRSEC record, and it comes back on the screen verbatim in USRTYPEO.\n\nThe read succeeds and the rewrite succeeds, so there are two sends - 'Press PF5 key to save your updates ...' in DFHNEUTR from the read, then 'User USER0004 has been updated ...' in DFHGREEN, composed by the STRING at :372-375 with SEC-USR-ID DELIMITED BY SPACE.",
